/-! The penta opening image (696 words, no image data) and its symbolic program.

Registers: `x8` index pointer, `x9` trapdoor, `x18` positions left, `x19 = 5`, `x20` proof start,
`x21` output cursor, `x22` salt base, `x23 = 368`. Per position: load the index into `x6`, copy the
16-byte salt, then for each level `k = 0 … 10` (with `x6 = index / 5^k`): `x24 = x6 / 5`,
`x25 = x6 % 5`, `x30` = trapdoor + group base `k` + 40 + 368 `x24`, and the four other children
`x30 + 32 ((x25 + j + 1) % 5)` (`j = 0 … 3`) are copied with doubleword loads/stores; then
`x6 = x24`. No footer. -/

